
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

## SyncBoard hardware I/O tests

`test_hardware_io.py` sends real output commands. It is skipped by default and
requires an explicit opt-in plus the output identifiers that are safe for the
current wiring. The tests drive each selected output low, high, then low and
attempt to leave the whole board disabled even on failure.

Run it only with an isolated or otherwise safe test setup:

```bash
SYNCBOARD_HARDWARE_TESTS=1 \\
SYNCBOARD_TEST_DO_CHANNEL=1 \\
SYNCBOARD_TEST_GPIO=13 \\
python3 -m unittest discover -s test -p 'test_hardware_io.py' -v
```

The test discovers the SyncBoard via `syncboard/com.py` (VID:PID
`16C0:0483`). Set `SYNCBOARD_PORT` to override discovery for a multi-device
rig.

The board's framed acknowledgement verifies that each command was received and
executed. For an electrical assertion, connect the selected output to suitable
measurement equipment or a deliberately wired loopback.
